/*
 * Engineering **blueprints** — per grade, the stat modifiers a blueprint applies AND
 * the materials one roll costs. Keyed by the blueprint's Frontier `fdname` — the string a
 * Loadout event's `Engineering.BlueprintName` carries, for 79 of the 109. The three that
 * share a journal id with another record carry a `journalName` saying so; the other 27 are
 * the Operations keys, for which no journal spelling has been observed. See the
 * note below.
 *
 * Sources: EDCD/coriolis-data, modifications/blueprints.json (commit 0db9234b5b9ce8c939ea84133d7ce336eea88e27)
 *          https://github.com/EDCD/coriolis-data `features` from the blueprint grade +
 *          modifications.json apply method; journal Labels resolved via EDSY
 *          (github.com/taleden/EDSY, CC BY-NC 4.0). `materials` from the grade's
 *          `components`, display names resolved to material `symbol`s against the
 *          materials domain. The two scanner `journalName` fields rest on EDSY edsy.js,
 *          whose `Build.fromJournal` resolves a journal `BlueprintName` through a
 *          per-module-type map (`fdevmap.mtypeBlueprint[mtypeid][fdname]`) — the evidence
 *          that one id can name two recipes, read alongside eddb.js's own `cs_lr` /
 *          `scan_lr` rows sharing the fdname `Sensor_LongRange`. Acquired 2026-08-06 UTC
 *          from raw.githubusercontent.com/taleden/EDSY/master/edsy.js, SHA-256
 *          a40e9bbe65d482a029527d6dc2abdbd1819672e5a5d4a3a4d88ea411f02575f5; the eddb.js
 *          read with it is byte-identical to the snapshot the other passes pin (967834d6…,
 *          internal `db 20260428`). Same CC BY-NC 4.0 terms. The game logic is Elite
 *          Dangerous data, property of Frontier Developments plc, under Frontier's
 *          media-usage terms: https://forums.frontier.co.uk/threads/510879/
 *
 * Each blueprint is { name, grades }. `name` is the blueprint's short modifier label
 * (coriolis `blueprint.name` for the journal-keyed ones; the Operations dossier's
 * display label for the Operations ones), deliberately NOT the full outfitting-panel
 * string — the panel says "Long-Range Weapon" where this says "Long range", because
 * the name is read next to the module it applies to. `CargoRack_IncreasedCapacity` is
 * the one name that is short-by-nothing rather than short by convention: it reads
 * "Expanded Cargo Rack", EDSY's spelling. See the "Display names" note in SOURCES.md.
 * `journalName` is present on the three blueprints whose key is not what the game writes
 * **and whose journal spelling another record already uses** — it marks a collision, not
 * merely a rename. It is absent from the other 106 records.
 *
 * **The journal spelling is the key wherever the game publishes one.** A registry name is
 * kept only as an alias that still resolves: `GuardianModule_Sturdy` is what a Loadout
 * writes for Anti-Guardian Zone Resistance — on Guardian weapons as well as modules — so
 * that is the key all nine offering menus list, and the registry's
 * `recipe_guardianmodule_sturdy` and `recipe_guardianweapon_sturdy` are stored beside it
 * so a build carrying either still looks up. Of the remaining 25 Operations keys, 21
 * belong to modules sold already engineered and four are Operations recipes a player rolls
 * at an engineer ("Four Operations recipes are listed by a menu" in SOURCES.md); no
 * journal spelling has been observed for any of them, which is not the same as knowing the
 * game writes none. Two of the exceptions are `Scanner_LongRange` and `Scanner_WideAngle`:
 * the game writes `Sensor_LongRange` / `Sensor_WideAngle` for the utility scanners' Long
 * Range and Wide Angle *and* for the sensor suites' own, which are different recipes
 * rolling different stats — EDSY's `scan_lr` and `cs_lr` are two rows under one fdname,
 * and its journal importer disambiguates by module type. coriolis splits the scanner side
 * out under these keys and this file follows it, because two recipes need two records;
 * `journalName` is how a reader gets back to the id a journal actually carries. Which of
 * the two a given id means is a question only the fitted module can answer — see
 * `resolveBlueprintForModule` in `ships/blueprint-journal`, and §Scanner Long Range and
 * Wide Angle in SOURCES.md. The third is `MC_Overcharged`, the same shape on the
 * multi-cannons: coriolis-data splits Overcharged into a multi-cannon key carrying an
 * `AmmoClipSize` leg and the `Weapon_Overcharged` every other weapon takes, gives both the
 * fdname `Weapon_Overcharged`, and lists the multi-cannon one on its `mc` and `advmc`
 * groups alone. A journal capture holds the clip-less side down: a large gimballed cannon
 * rolled to grade 5 under this id reports no `AmmoClipSize` modifier and a full magazine,
 * where a recipe that charges a clip states the leg. EDSY's single Overcharged carries the
 * clip leg on every weapon, and is the reading not followed here. See §Multi-cannon
 * Overcharged in SOURCES.md.
 *
 * `grades` maps grade "1".."5" to { features, materials }.
 * A feature is { label, method, min, max }: `label` the journal Modifier Label, `method`
 * how it applies ("multiplicative" -> base*(1+v), "additive" -> base+v, "overwrite" -> v),
 * [min, max] bounding the value by the quality roll (v = min + (max-min)*quality). A
 * material is { symbol, name, count }: join `symbol` to the materials domain for the
 * material's own grade and category. A grade may have an empty `materials` list
 * (CargoRack_IncreasedCapacity G5).
 *
 * The Operations pre-engineered blueprints (Merc weapon rewards, plus
 * general/core/optional ones like `FuelScoop_Efficiency`) and all three Anti-Guardian
 * records (`GuardianModule_Sturdy` and its two `recipe_`-prefixed Inara aliases, which
 * coriolis does not carry under any spelling) come from the current in-game / Inara
 * blueprint registry, which exposes one displayed total per grade rather than a
 * roll-bounded range: each such feature stores that total as a fixed value (min == max).
 * Their per-roll `materials` are from the same registry (a Merc-Coin amount is also
 * charged but is a currency, not a material, so it is not stored). Some of their totals
 * are non-monotonic (pre-engineered UI values, not primitive weights) and are preserved as
 * published, not "corrected".
 *
 * Full provenance: data/ships/SOURCES.md.
 */
